    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Complete Ingredient List</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">According to Costco's product information, the Kirkland Signature hot dog contains:</p>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-5 my-6">
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700">
          <li><strong>Beef</strong> — USDA Choice grade (the primary ingredient)</li>
          <li><strong>Water</strong> — for texture and moisture</li>
          <li><strong>Salt</strong> — for flavor enhancement</li>
          <li><strong>Corn syrup solids</strong> — for sweetness and moisture retention (contains ≤2%)</li>
          <li><strong>Dextrose</strong> — a sugar derived from corn (≤2%)</li>
          <li><strong>Spices</strong> — proprietary blend (≤2%)</li>
          <li><strong>Paprika</strong> — for color (≤2%)</li>
          <li><strong>Sodium erythorbate</strong> — a preservative (≤2%)</li>
          <li><strong>Sodium nitrite</strong> — a preservative and color fixative (≤2%)</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">That's it. Nine ingredients, all clearly listed. No artificial colors or flavors. No pork derivatives. No poultry. No fillers like soy protein or wheat.</p>
